<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base up 1.97 pct in Oct 11 week.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base up 1.97 pct in Oct 11 week.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base grew 1.97 percent to 2.78 billion sucres in the week to October 11, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>The bank did not explain the reasons for the increase.</p>
<p>In the previous week, monetary base grew 6.6 percent.</p>
<p>The monetary base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
</text>
